1444], "windows": [[44435, 45034], [45035, 45634], [45635, 46234], [46235, 46834]]}, "result_digest": "c22aa442b79c0e02", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [44435, 45034]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [45035, 45634]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [45635, 46234]}, {\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [46235, 46834]}]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 36205, "tokens_after": 36205, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_15", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 1962, "direction": "in", "window": [45635, 46834]}, "result_digest": "99b45369aa5a54b0", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"in\", \"n_neighbors\": 0, \"neighbors\": [], \"node\": 1962, \"window\": [45635, 46834]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 44726, "tokens_after": 44726, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "neighbors", "args": {"node": 563, "direction": "out", "window": [45635, 46834]}, "result_digest": "696695b75b8ffc39", "result_summary": "{\"direction\": \"out\", \"n_neighbors\": 8, \"neighbors\": [171, 178, 282, 397, 715, 949, 1157, 1926], \"node\": 563, \"window\": [45635, 46834]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 44726, "tokens_after": 44726, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_a439d8df", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [563, 1444], "window": [20435, 58834], "confidence": 0.72, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "563's activity is back-loaded and 1444's inbound activity is front-loaded, so the temporal ordering runs the wrong way for most of the interval. In the only overlapping period, 1444 has a single inbound contact (from 1962), and 1962 itself receives nothing in the preceding 600 units, so that final hop cannot terminate a \u0394t\u2264600 chain from 563. The static 2-hop connectivity and the high event volume of both nodes are confounders, not evidence of influence flow."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**Temporal evidence:**\n\n1. **Reversed activity profiles (step_06, step_07):** Node 563's outgoing activity is concentrated *late* in the interval (1, 0, 1, 3, 3, 13, 18, 28 events across octiles \u2014 59 of 67 events after t\u224844435), while node 1444's incoming activity is concentrated *early* (30, 17, 10, 5, 3, 1, 0, 0 \u2014 57 of 66 events before t\u224834834). The source ramps up essentially after the target has gone quiet.\n\n2. **The late-window bottleneck (step_12):** In [42035, 58834] \u2014 the only period where 563 is substantially active \u2014 node 1444 receives from exactly **one** node, 1962, and that single event falls in [46235, 46834] (step_14).\n\n3. **The bottleneck has no feeder (step_15, step_16):** Node 1962 received **zero** incoming edges in [45635, 46834], i.e. in the 600-unit window preceding its contact with 1444. So the 1962\u21921444 hop cannot be the tail of any \u0394t\u2264600 chain. Meanwhile 563's out-contacts in that same window (171, 178, 282, 397, 715, 949, 1157, 1926 \u2014 step_16) do not include 1962.\n\n4. **Confounder controls:** High volume and high degree are present but misleading \u2014 both nodes have ~66 events and 65+ distinct partners (step_02), and a static 2-hop neighbourhood around 563 is dense (step_05). Yet 563's early-window out-neighbourhood is only 7 nodes (step_10), disjoint from 1444's 64 in-neighbours (step_11). Connectivity when time is ignored is not matched by any ordered, gap-respecting path.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_a439d8df\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [563, 1444],\n  \"window\": [20435, 58834],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"563's activity is back-loaded and 1444's inbound activity is front-loaded, so the temporal ordering runs the wrong way for most of the interval. In the only overlapping period, 1444 has a single inbound contact (from 1962), and 1962 itself receives nothing in the preceding 600 units, so that final hop cannot terminate a \u0394t\u2264600 chain from 563. The static 2-hop connectivity and the high event volume of both nodes are confounders, not evidence of influence flow.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53624, "total_output_tokens": 6976, "total_tokens": 60600, "total_latency_ms": 102271, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}